{"groups":[{"members":["c1","c2","c3","c4"],"primary":"c3","title":"Prohibition of Anti-Competitive Automated Rent Price-Fixing Ordinance","requirement":"It is unlawful to sell, license or otherwise provide an algorithmic device to a landlord, and unlawful for a landlord to use one to set rental rates or occupancy levels for residential rental property. An algorithmic device is software that uses nonpublic competitor data to recommend rents or occupancy levels. Tenants may sue for injunctive relief, damages or civil penalties, plus costs and reasonable attorney's fees.","key_value":"Civil penalties up to $1,000 per violation; each month of use and each affected property is a separate violation","status":"in_force","effective_date":null,"end_date":null,"citation":"San Diego Mun. Code §§ 98.1101–98.1104","coverage_conditions":"All residential rental property in the City of San Diego; applies to landlords and to persons who sell, license, or provide algorithmic devices.","exemptions":"(a) Reports on rental rates or occupancy levels built from aggregated nonpublic competitor data more than 90 days old, or from publicly available information, that do not recommend rates or occupancy levels for future leases or renewals; (b) software used to set rents or income limits under local, state or federal affordable housing program guidelines.","coverage_from":"c3","conflict_note":"Status conflict. The official source D076 (c3) is a proposed-ordinance document with no adoption shown, so it reports status 'pending'. The secondary sources D002 (c1), D037 (c2) and D086 (c4) report the ban as enacted and in force; c1 and c2 give an effective date of June 2025 (month only). Status is set to in_force because D076 predates adoption and does not contradict it. The exact effective date is unverified in official text, so it is left null."}],"dropped":[]}
